          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow section-label"><span>01 /</span> Open Science Labs</p>
              <h2 id="osl-title">Open-source tools<br />and infrastructure.</h2>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://opensciencelabs.org/projects/incubation/"
                >Explore the OSL Incubator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
            <p>
              At OSL, we helped develop and maintain projects in its incubator
              community. The program supports open-source projects working
              toward sustainable maintenance. Highlights from our work include:
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="engagement-grid">
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 01 ] Automation</span>
              <h3>Makim</h3>
              <p>A task runner for repeatable development and research workflows,
                configured in YAML.</p>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://makim.org/"
                >Explore Makim <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 02 ] Containers</span>
              <h3>Sugar</h3>
              <p>A tool for simplifying container workflows and managing
                configurations across environments.</p>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sugar-org/sugar"
                >Explore Sugar <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 03 ] Literature data</span>
              <h3>PyMedX</h3>
              <p>A Python library for accessing PubMed, continued as a fork
                of the archived PyMed project.</p>
              <div class="inline-links">
                <a href="https://github.com/osl-incubator/pymedx">PyMedX ↗</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/gijswobben/pymed">Original PyMed ↗</a>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div class="section-note">
            <span class="note-symbol" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            <p>
              We created and maintained OSL’s technical infrastructure: bots,
              continuous integration, websites, plugins, and DevOps workflows,
              alongside smaller support tools used across its projects.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/OpenScienceLabs"
              >OSL on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            >
